# ── never ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.DS_Store
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.Renviron
*.log

# Claude Code local state (settings, caches). The committed CLAUDE.md at the
# repo root is the shared contract; .claude/ is per-machine.
.claude/

# ── out/: renders, not committed ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Same rule as the other repos: if a script can rebuild it, it is not
# committed. A spec + its committed data JSON + this code reproduce any mp4
# exactly, so the mp4 is derived output. mp4 is also already-compressed
# binary that git cannot delta: every re-render of the same video stores a
# full new blob. At 2-3 videos/week for a year that is several hundred MB of
# undeltifiable history for files we can regenerate in seconds.
out/

# ── src/data/*.json: deliberately NOT ignored ────────────────────────────
# These look derived but are not reproducible. FRED revises: re-running
# fetch.R six months from now returns different numbers than the vintage a
# published video actually showed. The JSON plus its .meta.json sidecar is
# the vintage record of what went on screen. A few KB each. Nothing above
# matches src/data/, so they are tracked; keep it that way.
